  (text "SAO++ power select: the switch common feeds the LED. Position 1 = badge 3.3 V, position 2 = OFF (pin 2 unconnected), position 3 = coin cell." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 38.1 38.1 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "ae02ac58-b10a-5bc5-9076-389f6ac39afe"))
  (text "The badge supply and the coin cell sit on separate switch contacts and are never connected to each other." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 38.1 41.91 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "9406a1b6-8279-560c-b7be-ae881612f9bb"))
  (text "LED-only board: SDA, SCL, GPIO1 and GPIO2 are not connected, so no series diode is needed on the cell (see docs/standard.md section 3)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 38.1 45.72 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "da90c93d-c056-54ea-9550-94d8f157cd84"))
  (text "D1 is the red light in the middle of the sheriff's star: reverse-mount, shining through the board. 1.3 k gives about 1 mA." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 38.1 124.46 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "503d440e-119d-564f-82ae-fc78076c180c"))
  (text "The maker's board had a 5 mm through-hole LED there, a 1 k resistor, and a solder jumper 'LED SELECT' (badge VCC or badge GPIO2)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 38.1 128.27 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "0b1aafa3-ec30-5bb2-98c2-55e2c2ba6eeb"))
  (text "That jumper is gone: the switch chooses the supply, and GPIO2 is left unconnected." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 38.1 132.08 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "aade0535-bb44-5c37-8b92-94e1bcfe8209"))
